      {
        "id": 225934,
        "name": "Blackfang108",
        "username": "Blackfang108",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/74df32/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2019-03-13T19:14:31.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Powerhound_2000\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/48/1859_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Powerhound_2000:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Chilly Steke wrote:</b>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Powerhound_2000 wrote:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I would say thematically the idea is not that Wraith is shooting a stun bolt just once.&nbsp; When you use that power as long as Wraith is around that target she is continuing to hit that target. &nbsp; When she leaves for another Battle Zone she isn’t hitting them anymore but if they together again she continues with her spray of Stun Bolts. &nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>If that were the case, then if Wraith were incapacitated, she would stop her barrage of Stun Bolts, and the effect would stop. Which it doesn’t… suggesting that it was just one Stun Bolt. Either way you slice it, thematically it certainly does seem to be inconsistent/nonsensical.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</div>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>We’ve been told being incapped doesn’t mean the hero is dead. &nbsp; They are still trying to help. &nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>If she gets removed from the game by, e.g. Final Wasteland eating her, the effect still continues until her turn would have been.&nbsp;so - thematically it certainly does seem to be inconsistent/nonsensical.</p>",
